---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/post-purchase';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/post-purchase');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/post-purchase');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Post-purchase education</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify SMS and email: post-purchase education</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">Anchor education to fulfillment and actual product use. This guide sets out selection criteria and proposed workflows; it does not report hands-on platform tests or merchant campaign results.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-16 space-y-8">
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Separate order service from marketing</h2>
      <p>Receipts, tracking and delivery exception notices have a different job from cross-sells. Maintain an owner for each service notification so the marketing platform does not duplicate Shopify or shipping-provider messages. Use email for detailed care instructions and SMS for a useful short update only when the message and channel are permitted. A completed purchase does not itself grant marketing consent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Supplier fit: Klaviyo order-triggered flows</h2>
      <p>Klaviyo documents post-purchase flows triggered by a placed order through an integrated ecommerce platform. This supports evaluating an order-driven education sequence; it does not establish that every carrier delivery event or gift flag is present. Inspect the events in the store account before selecting a delivery-based trigger or promising product-specific branches.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Define the event map</h2>
      <p>Map order ID, purchased variants, fulfillment status, delivery status when available, gift indicator, return state and consent by channel. Treat split shipments independently: a fulfilled accessory must not start instructions for a backordered main product. If delivery is unavailable, label the timing as estimated and use tracking confirmation before asking for a review.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Three proposed merchant workflows</h2>
      <p>Skincare: link approved product instructions after shipment, then check whether help is needed after delivery before suggesting another product. Candles: let explicit gift buyers receive shareable care guidance without enrolling recipients. Outdoor gear: send assembly instructions for the purchased equipment, with a support route before a complementary accessory offer. No return reduction, repeat-purchase gain or ticket result is claimed for these designs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Use a timeline with exceptions</h2>
      <p>A draft sequence could provide shipment guidance, a usage check three days after confirmed delivery, a review invitation after a realistic use period and a later complementary offer. Those delays require category-specific validation. Digital activation may happen immediately; apparel needs a fit and return window; preorders need expectation updates during the wait. Do not send a review request merely because seven days passed after checkout.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Gift and bundle branches</h2>
      <p>Use an explicit gift selection where possible; a different shipping address is an imperfect signal, not proof. Do not add a gift recipient to marketing because a buyer entered their address. Bundle education should be one coherent guide instead of three SKU emails arriving together. Combine line-item instructions and apply an agreed contact cap across review, loyalty and replenishment flows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Pause selling when support is unresolved</h2>
      <p>Suppress optional cross-sells and review requests during a return, cancellation or unresolved delivery issue. Keep necessary service updates available through the responsible service system. Build content around frequent setup and tracking questions, linking to current instructions and support. Supplement or skincare education should use approved usage language rather than new health claims.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
      <p>Create draft tests for split fulfillment, cancellation, full refund, gift purchase, bundle and missing delivery event. Replay an event to check duplicate prevention. Confirm that a queued cross-sell is skipped after a return and that a missing product guide uses a safe fallback. These are proposed account exercises; no live integration or messaging test was performed for this guide.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Measure customer success as well as sales</h2>
      <p>Report support tickets per delivered order, education-link use, returns by product, second-order contribution and opt-outs. Separate service and promotional messages in reporting. A fall in tickets alone could reflect inaccessible support, so read ticket reasons and customer feedback. Review the handoff to replenishment only after product timing and delivery data are stable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card prose-shopify">
      <h2>Primary supplier reference</h2>
      <p>Checked 25 November 2026: <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360028872611">Klaviyo post-purchase flow documentation</a>. The supplier fact above is limited to that documented capability. The workflow rules and acceptance exercises are editorial proposals for a merchant to validate.</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold" aria-label="Related guides">
      <a class="link" href="/use-cases/holiday-gifting">Holiday gifting →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory →</a>
    </nav>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
